  <text>
      <body>
         <entry xml:id="qatedrin-dlgenr"
            xml:lang="en"
            type="mainEntry"
            prev="#"
            next="#"
            source="Genesis Rabbah">
            <form type="lemma" opt="false">
               <orth type="lemma" xml:lang="jpa" opt="false" select="true">קתדרין</orth>
               <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb" opt="false">qtdryn</orth>
               <pron notation="rabbinic" opt="false">qatedrin</pron>
               <gramGrp opt="false">
                  <gram type="pos" opt="false">noun</gram>
                  <gram type="gen">m.</gram>
               </gramGrp>
            </form>
            <sense xml:id="qatedrin-dlgenr-1">
               <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en" subtype="sense">
                  <quote>cathedra, throne</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="translationEquivalent" xml:lang="grc">
                  <quote>καθέδριον</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="example" xml:lang="jpa">
                  <quote>ויקח לו את כל אלה וגו' ר' יהודה א' שרי אומות העולם הראה לו, ר' נחמיה א' שרי ישראל הראה לו, על דעתיה דר' יודה קתדרין דדין כל קבל קתדרין דדין, על דעתיה דר' נחמיה ששם היתה סנהדרין גדולה שלישראל יושבת וחותכת דיניהן שלישראל</quote>
                  <bibl>
                     <ref type="witness">44,15</ref>
                     <ref type="witness">I 438: 1</ref>
                  </bibl>
                  <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                     <quote>And he took him all these (Gen 15,10). R. Yehuda said: He showed him the princes of the Gentile nations. R. Neḥemiah said: He showed him the princes of Israel. On the view of R. Yehuda, the throne of one [prince] opposing the throne of another. According to R. Neḥemiah, it symbolised the place where the great Sanhedrin [Court] of Israel sat and determined the laws of Israel. (Freedman / Simon I 371)</quote>
                  </cit>
                  <note>= <bibl type="ancient">Yalq 77 [I 307: 65;66]</bibl></note>
               </cit>
            </sense>
            <note>Attested also in <bibl type="ancient">yYom 4,1 [578: 36]</bibl>. Cf. <bibl type="modern">AC VII 228a</bibl> (sub <term xml:lang="jpa">קתדרא</term>); <bibl type="modern">Levi IV 402b</bibl>; <bibl type="modern">Jastrow II 1434a</bibl>. The form <term xml:lang="jpa">קתדרא</term> <term xml:lang="fjb">qtdrʾ</term> <term xml:lang="rabbinic">qatedraʾ</term> (not in GenR) is attested in <bibl type="ancient">mKet 5,5</bibl> (cf. <bibl type="modern">Heijmanns [2013] 228-229</bibl>) and many other Rabbinic sources.</note>
            <ref type="bibliography">
               <bibl>
                  <title>Krauss, LW II</title>
                  <citedRange>572b</citedRange>
               </bibl>
            </ref>
         </entry>
